{"id":"chatcmpl-e23c7712-f3a4-4fd0-aa46-b1dc57ef0aa3","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251541,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a conflict-resolution pattern for medical image interpretation where multiple specialized models disagree. The strategy involves triangulating evidence from independent expert models, using targeted region-of-interest inspection to verify anatomical findings, and explicitly auditing conflicting outputs before committing to an answer. The key insight is that laterality and subtle findings (like small effusions) require focused anatomical reasoning rather than majority voting.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple expert models disagree on a finding, obtain a third independent opinion and explicitly document the conflict before finalizing.\",\n    \"For subtle or laterality-dependent findings, direct model attention to specific anatomical landmarks (e.g., costophrenic angles) rather than asking global questions.\",\n    \"Use region-of-interest cropping/zooming to verify ambiguous findings that drive the final answer, especially when models conflict.\",\n    \"Prefer anatomically-grounded reasoning (landmark blunting, meniscus signs) over simple majority vote when resolving model disagreements.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image QA\": \"Ask models about specific anatomical landmarks rather than global impressions; cross-validate with at least two independent models; use ROI inspection to confirm subtle findings.\",\n    \"Conflicting model outputs\": \"When models disagree, gather a third opinion, then reason from anatomical evidence rather than vote-counting; document the conflict explicitly.\",\n    \"Laterality determination\": \"Focus queries on side-specific landmarks (diaphragm height, spine overlay, angle blunting) since lateral views require anatomical inference rather than direct left/right labeling.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Before answering, confirm whether all consulted models agree; if not, obtain an additional independent opinion and inspect the relevant ROI.\",\n    \"Verify that the final answer is supported by a specific anatomical sign (e.g., posterior costophrenic blunting) rather than only model consensus.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":843,"total_tokens":1232,"completion_tokens":389,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":843},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":389}}}